{"tool_name":"md_davis","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"md_davis","home":"https://github.com/djmaity/md-davis/tree/v0.4.0","license":"MIT","summary":"Interactive Data Visualization of Protein Molecular Dynamics.","addition_date":"2022-08-28T00:06:30.690520Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:46:32.694863Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:md_davis","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"dpal@iisc.ac.in","name":"Debnath Pal","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3591-5978","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Dibyajyoti Maity","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8032-646X"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://md-davis.readthedocs.io"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2476"},{"term":"Protein geometry calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0249"},{"term":"Simulation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0244"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"MD DaVis","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac314","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: Molecular dynamics (MD) simulations have become an integral part of biomolecular study. Most MD software suites do not include analysis tools and those which do create very basic visualizations. Molecular Dynamics Data Visualizer (MD DaVis) is a python package developed to facilitate quick comparative analysis of MD trajectories of similar proteins or the same protein under different conditions. MD DaVis can quickly generate interactive visualization from molecular dynamics trajectories with a few simple steps. Interactive plots eliminate the need to make multiple plots for comparison, improving productivity and saving time.","authors":[{"name":"Maity D."},{"name":"P